! v0.74.0 PCM test 6:  three-model comparison on water in benzene.
!
! Same molecule, same geometry, same basis, three solvent models.
! Benzene (eps = 2.27) is the cleanest case to see the conductor-
! approximation breakdown: C-PCM treats it as a near-conductor
! (f = 0.5595) which is way off, while IEFPCM keeps the full
! dielectric law.  COSMO's empirical (eps-1)/(eps+0.5) = 0.4496
! sits in between.
!
! Reference numbers harvested in v0.74.0 commit:
!   IEFPCM:  G_pol = -0.002629800277
!
! This test runs the C-PCM half; the runner pairs it with the
! IEFPCM benzene test for the divergence assertion.
%method  HF
%basis   sto-3g
%job     energy
%pcm     cpcm
%eps     2.2706
%geom angstrom
O  0.000000   0.000000   0.119262
H  0.000000   0.755453  -0.477047
H  0.000000  -0.755453  -0.477047
*end
